2. THE PROBLEMS WITH TRADITIONAL pip WORKFLOWS
============================================================

Traditional Python development commonly uses separate tools for different tasks.

Although these tools work well, managing them individually can sometimes become inconvenient.

2.1 Slow Package Installation

Installing packages with pip can take time, especially when:

- Installing multiple dependencies.
- Resolving complex dependency requirements.
- Working with large projects.
- Reinstalling packages in different environments.

2.2 Confusing Virtual Environment Commands

Python developers often need to remember multiple commands.

Example:

    python -m venv .venv

    # Windows
    .venv\Scripts\activate

    # macOS / Linux
    source .venv/bin/activate

    pip install requests

These commands work, but beginners may find environment creation and activation confusing.

2.3 Different Tools for Different Tasks

Traditional Python development may involve several tools:

- pip: Package installation.
- venv: Virtual environment creation.
- pip-tools: Dependency compilation and management.
- pyenv: Python version management.

Using multiple tools can make project setup more complicated.

2.4 Environment Management Problems

Common problems include:

- Installing packages into the wrong Python environment.
- Dependency version conflicts.
- Inconsistent development environments.
- Difficulty reproducing another developer's setup.
- Forgetting to update dependency files.

Modern tools such as uv help simplify these workflows.

