3. WHY IS uv SO FAST?
============================================================

uv uses several performance optimizations to make Python package management faster.

3.1 Written in Rust

uv is written in Rust, a compiled programming language designed for performance and memory safety.

This helps uv execute package-management operations efficiently.

3.2 Smart Caching

uv maintains a cache of downloaded packages and related files.

When the same packages are needed again, uv can reuse cached data instead of downloading everything again.

Benefits:

- Reduces repeated downloads.
- Saves installation time.
- Improves repeated project setup.

3.3 Parallel Downloads

uv can download multiple packages concurrently.

This reduces the waiting time compared with downloading packages one after another.

3.4 Optimized Dependency Resolution

Python projects may require many packages with different version requirements.

uv uses an optimized dependency resolver to find compatible package versions efficiently.

These features together contribute to uv's performance.

